' System block diagram — the whole platform in one view.
' Two transports are deliberately separated: request/response over internal
' HTTP with a shared secret, and fire-and-forget domain events over RabbitMQ.
'
' LAYOUT — READ BEFORE REARRANGING. smetana gives no direct control over rank
' or column, so the three tricks below are what keep the edges untangled. They
' were arrived at by rendering every ordering and counting edge crossings in
' the SVG; the arrangement here scores 12 crossings, the worst one scores 22.
'
'   1. NO PACKAGE AROUND THE INFRASTRUCTURE. Boxing PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ,
'      MinIO and LiveKit together forces all four onto one rank, which is what
'      produced the long horizontal runs across the old version. Left loose,
'      each one settles next to the services that actually use it.
'   2. THE HIDDEN `right` CHAINS fix left-to-right order inside a package.
'      The .NET order below is load-bearing: ClassroomService is the hub (it
'      reaches five other nodes) so it sits centrally, and EmailService sits
'      directly above RabbitMQ because that is its only edge.
'   3. THE HIDDEN `down` EDGES into the external box push it onto a rank of its
'      own. Without them it lands beside PostgreSQL and MinIO, which widens
'      the diagram — and a wider diagram is a SMALLER diagram on the page,
'      since the figure is scaled to \textwidth either way.
'
' The external group is a dashed rectangle rather than a `cloud`: PlantUML
' underestimates a cloud's bounding box and the wavy outline gets clipped off
' the bottom edge of the PNG.
@startuml
!include _style.puml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
hide stereotype
skinparam rectangle<<external>> {
  BorderStyle dashed
  BorderColor #555555
}

package "الواجهة الأمامية" {
  [React 19 + Vite\nSPA] as SPA
}

node "بوابة nginx" as GW

package "خدمات .NET" {
  [UserManagementService\nالهوية والأدوار] as UMS
  [ClassroomService\nالفصول والجلسات والاختبارات] as CS
  [StreamingService\nغرف البث والتسجيل] as SS
  [EmailService\nمستهلك أحداث فقط] as ES
  UMS -[hidden]right- CS
  CS -[hidden]right- SS
  SS -[hidden]right- ES
}

node "LiveKit\nSFU + Egress + Redis" as LK
database "PostgreSQL ×5\nقاعدة لكل خدمة" as PG
queue "RabbitMQ\nMassTransit" as MQ
storage "MinIO / S3\nتسجيلات وملخصات وملفات" as S3

package "خدمات الذكاء (Python / FastAPI)" {
  [RagService\nالفهرسة والاسترجاع RAG] as KS
  [LiveAssistantService\nتحويل الكلام والتحليل] as LAS
  KS -[hidden]right- LAS
}

rectangle "خدمات خارجية" <<external>> {
  [Gemini\nتوليد وتضمين] as GEM
  [Groq\nتحويل الكلام إلى نص] as GRQ
  GEM -[hidden]right- GRQ
}

SPA --> GW : HTTPS
SPA ..> LK : **WebRTC**\n(لا يمر عبر البوابة)

GW --> SS
GW --> UMS
GW --> CS

SS --> LK : واجهة\nLiveKit
' Both Python services are reached the same way; labelling one arrow keeps the
' two labels from colliding under the .NET box.
CS --> KS : HTTP داخلي\n+ سر مشترك
CS --> LAS

SS --> MQ
UMS --> MQ
CS --> MQ
MQ --> ES : أحداث المجال

SS --> PG
UMS --> PG
CS --> PG
KS --> PG
LAS --> PG

LK --> S3 : تسجيل MP4
CS --> S3
KS --> S3

PG -[hidden]down- GRQ
S3 -[hidden]down- GEM

KS --> GEM
LAS --> GEM
LAS --> GRQ
@enduml
